response:
The incident involves the threat group UAC-0035 (InvisiMole) targeting government bodies in Ukraine using phishing emails containing a ZIP archive. The archive executes an LNK file to download and run an HTA file, which drops a decoy document and the backdoor malware LoadEdge (EdgeNotification.dll). LoadEdge can deploy further malware from the group's arsenal, such as TunnelMole and RC2CL. C2 infrastructure is hosted on IP 45.95.11.34.

